  "narrative": "I corrected the previous registration error by linking refinements only to claims with available motivating evidence. The accepted dataset-level findings are H6, H8, and H20, so the most informative refinements test whether their effects persist after restricting to technical, p53, MSI, or histology contexts. For H6, I registered the MSI-high versus WRN dependency effect within Avana-library screens and within TP53-intact screens to assess whether the huge WRN effect is robust and not driven by library or p53-loss context. For H8, I registered the validated SMARCA4-loss versus SMARCA2 effect within screen_batch and Avana-library subsets to test technical robustness. For H20, I registered the reversed KEAP1/NFE2L2 effect in TP53-intact and MSI-intact subsets to test whether the unexpected weaker NFE2L2 dependency in KEAP1-loss cells persists in cleaner genomic contexts. The borderline KRAS and EGFR oncogene-addiction claims are refined to adenocarcinoma because these lesions are expected to be more dominant in that context. Finally, I added standalone specificity variants for NF1 loss on KRAS dependency within KRAS-mutation-free cells and BRCA2 loss on WRN dependency within MSI-intact cells; these are not marked as parent-linked refinements because the parent claims H13 and H14 currently have no evidence.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted dataset findings: H6 active, H8 closed after validation, H20 active. Corrected refine-only-where-parent-has-evidence. Proposed refinements prioritize robustness and specificity of accepted findings, then adenocarcinoma restriction for borderline KRAS/EGFR effects, and parentless specificity variants for H13/H14. In analyze, prefer new evidence-producing claims among H13-H19 and these refinements; avoid rerunning accepted claims unless validation or refinement adds specificity. If H6 remains accepted, validate H6 before H20. If H20 validation is requested later, interpret as KEAP1-loss cells being less dependent on NFE2L2 within this dataset. Do not treat borderline H1/H4 as accepted without stronger evidence or a clinically meaningful effect size beyond uncertainty. Keep accepted claims dataset-associational, not causal or generalizable."
}

