  "narrative": "The due response for H6 is now fully supported. Discovery R6 and validation R52 both give direction-coded estimates of approximately +0.79 to +0.80 with 95% discovery interval +0.760 to +0.819 and independent stricter interval +0.753 to +0.851. The lower bound is far above the +0.10 clinical-significance benchmark, so MSI-high status is accepted as associated with much stronger WRN dependency in this dataset. With H8, H15, H20, H12, and H6 validation now assessed, the strongest supported dataset-level associations are four independent-validated central findings: MSI-high -> much stronger WRN dependency; SMARCA4 loss -> much stronger SMARCA2 dependency; KEAP1 loss -> much weaker NFE2L2 dependency; and TP53 loss -> much weaker USP7 dependency. The first two have lower bounds near +0.76 in discovery and +0.76 in validation, the third is similarly around +0.78 to +0.81, and USP7 has lower bounds near +0.29 to +0.33. These are robust within this supplied lung-lineage CRISPR dataset, but they are not causal claims or external generalizability claims.  Robustness is broad for the accepted contexts. The central associations persist across Avana and KY library contexts for several outcomes, across TP53, STK11, CDKN2A, and adenocarcinoma strata, and within MTAP-loss screens for TP53-loss/USP7. I now accept H45 and H67 as within-dataset subset confirmations: MSI-high/WRN among TP53-loss screens has signed +0.833 with lower bound +0.765, and MSI-high/WRN among CDKN2A-loss screens has signed +0.799 with lower bound +0.737. Both have small exposed cells, 24 and 21 respectively, so I retain a caution that these are supportive rather than primary claims, but their confidence intervals are entirely and substantially above the +0.10 threshold.  I also close many remaining small unresolved discovery claims because their signed intervals do not leave room for a clinically meaningful positive effect at the +0.10 benchmark. KRAS mutation/KRAS dependency, KRAS mutation interactions, EGFR amplification/EGFR dependency, ERBB2 amplification/ERBB2 dependency, TP53 loss/MDM2 dependency, MYC/KIF18A, BRCA2/WRN, KRAS/adenocarcinoma, EGFR/adenocarcinoma, USP7/CDKN2A loss, ARID1A interaction, NFE2L2 interactions, NFE2L2/STK11 strata, EGFR/TP53-intact, KRAS/STK11-intact, and MDM2/TP53-with-CDKN2A-intact all have upper signed bounds below +0.10 or effects far too small. These are negative or clinically uninformative within this dataset. The research marker screens are also noninformative for the central dependencies, with marker F/STAT3 independently validated as null.  The most useful unresolved items are not the central effects but context or interaction questions. H36, the WRN/MSI-high interaction within TP53-loss, remains unresolved because its interval spans the +0.10 benchmark. H80, TP53-loss/USP7 in KY-library screens, remains directionally supportive but uncertain because the lower bound is +0.051, below the threshold. The most informative next analyses are H85, the KY-library MSI-high/WRN check, to complete the technical robustness grid; H77, TMED10/STK11 loss, as a broad new outcome probe; and H23, SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 in batch_a, as an additional screen-batch robustness check. No new independent validation is needed for the four central associations, which are already validated, nor for the MTAP specificity checks, which are now closed as negative or confirmatory."
