  "narrative": "All 12 newly delivered comparisons use the signed +0.10 clinically meaningful benchmark on the hypothesis scale. H131, H133, H135, and H141 are accepted and closed: MSI-high cells show very strong WRN dependency at high mutation burden; PTEN-loss cells show strong STAT3 dependency at both high and low mutation burden; and KEAP1-loss cells show much weaker NFE2L2 dependency at high mutation burden. These are context robustness checks, not causal or generalizable claims. H140 is invalid because the low-burden exposed MSI-high cell has zero observations; I keep it unresolved but close it because the comparison is not evaluable in this dataset. H132 rejects a clinically meaningful positive WRN/MSI interaction by high mutation burden because the interval is entirely below the benchmark; the near-zero estimate provides no support for strong effect modification in the registered direction. H143 rejects the ARID1A-loss modification of SMARCA4/SMARCA2 and duplicates earlier evidence in values. H146 rejects a clinically meaningful positive ARID1A-loss modification of KEAP1/NFE2L2; the interval is far below +0.10 and also not meaningfully opposite. H134, H142, H144, and H145 remain unresolved: their point estimates are near zero or subbenchmark, intervals cross +0.10 or are wide; H142 has positive statistical evidence but only +0.076 point estimate, so any interaction is not established as clinically meaningful. They are deferred as low priority. I do not request validation: the large accepted effects already have independent validation, and the unresolved interactions are either small or underpowered, so validation intervals would likely be too imprecise to change the decision. Next, the active ARID1A-loss main effects H136-H139 remain useful as direct-context checks, and the new intermediate-burden WRN/MSI proposal fills the gap left by invalid H140. All conclusions are within-dataset associations.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 12 appraise. Operational rule: signed +0.10 benchmark; accept if lower >0.10, reject if upper <0.10, unresolved if crossing; absolute opposite meaningful only if interval entirely beyond -0.10. Central within-dataset associations stable and validated: WRN MSI-high, SMARCA2 SMARCA4 loss, NFE2L2 KEAP1 loss weaker, USP7 TP53 loss weaker, STAT3 PTEN loss stronger. Iter12 results: accept H131/R129 WRN MSI high burden; accept H133/R131 and H141/R135 STAT3 PTEN high/low burden; accept H135/R133 NFE2L2 KEAP1 high burden; invalid/close H140/R134 WRN MSI <=3 no exposed cell. Reject positive interactions: H132/R130 WRN MSI x high burden, H143/R137 SMARCA4 x ARID1A duplicate, H146/R140 NFE2L2 KEAP1 x ARID1A. Unresolved deferred interactions: H134/R132 STAT3 x high burden, H142/R136 WRN MSI x ARID1A small positive, H144/R138 STAT3 x ARID1A, H145/R139 USP7 TP53 x ARID1A. Keep H147-H149 deferred because high-burden battery did not reveal important heterogeneity. Keep H136-H139 active as direct ARID1A-loss context checks. New proposal: WRN MSI in mutation_burden 3 to <7 to clarify H140. No validation requested; validation budget preserved."
