  "narrative": "Final synthesis: I assessed the two due evidence responses and now support five large within-dataset associations, while closing the only remaining borderline heterogeneity claim. I maintain the operational signed +0.10 benchmark and require valid Welch cells. These conclusions are associations in this dataset, not causal mechanisms or external generalizability. First, MSI-high status is robustly associated with much stronger WRN dependency: H6 is accepted and independently validated by R52 (signed +0.802, 95% interval +0.753 to +0.851). This is stable across Avana (H21/R21), TP53 wild-type (H22/R22), adenocarcinoma (H35/R31), TP53 loss (H45/R41), STK11 wild-type (H49/R45), CDKN2A loss (H67/R63), KY library (H85/R80), batch_a (H86/R81), matched RNA-DNA-CRISPR QC (H89/R84), high mutation burden (H131/R129), ARID1A loss (H136/R141), and intermediate mutation burden (H150/R148). H132 rejects high-burden interaction, and H151 rejects adenocarcinoma interaction; H142 remains unresolved but is small. Second, SMARCA4 loss is robustly associated with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency: H8 is accepted and independently validated by R13 (+0.793, +0.763 to +0.822). It is stable across batch_a (H23/R78), Avana (H24/R23), TP53 loss (H46/R42), STK11 loss (H65/R61), CDKN2A loss (H66/R62), KY library (H78/R71), matched QC (H113/R110), adenocarcinoma (H119/R116), and ARID1A-loss context (H137/R142). ARID1A-loss interaction H143/R137 and high-burden interaction H147/R145 are rejected as sub-benchmark. Third, KEAP1 loss is robustly associated with much weaker NFE2L2 dependency: H20 is accepted and independently validated by R39 (+0.806, +0.775 to +0.838); the opposite stronger-dependency claim H9 is rejected. The association is broad across TP53 wild-type (H25/R24), MSS (H26/R25), Avana (H37/R33), adenocarcinoma (H38/R34), TP53 loss (H44/R40), STK11 wild-type (H47/R43), CDKN2A wild-type (H61/R64), STK11 loss (H64/R60), KY library (H79/R72), batch_a (H87/R82), matched QC (H114/R111), high mutation burden (H135/R133), ARID1A loss (H139/R144), and MTAP loss (H120/R117). TP53 interaction H39/R35, STK11 interaction H128/R125, ARID1A interaction H146/R140, and high-burden interaction H149/R147 are rejected. Fourth, TP53 loss is robustly associated with weaker USP7 dependency: H15 is accepted and independently validated by R26 (+0.395, +0.293 to +0.498). This is stable across Avana (H31/R29), CDKN2A wild-type (H40/R36), MSS (H48/R44), MTAP loss (H68/R55), KY library (H80/R73 and independent R91 +0.326, +0.106 to +0.546), batch_a (H88/R83), matched QC (H105/R102), adenocarcinoma (H115/R112), STK11 loss (H121/R118), and ARID1A loss (H138/R143). MTAP-loss main effects H58/R53 and H62/R54 are rejected, MTAP interaction H73/R57 is rejected, and the high-burden interaction H148 is now rejected. Fifth, PTEN loss is robustly associated with stronger STAT3 dependency: H93 is accepted and independently validated by R90 (+0.329, +0.255 to +0.402). It is stable across batch_a (H95/R92), adenocarcinoma (H97/R94), matched QC (H99/R96), PIK3CA mutant and wild-type (H100/R97, H101/R98), TP53 wild-type (H103/R100), KRAS mutant and wild-type (H107/R104, H108/R105), STK11 loss (H122/R119), KEAP1 loss (H123/R120), MTAP loss (H124/R121), 10% serum (H125/R122), high mutation burden (H133/R131), and intermediate mutation burden (H152/R150). The due validation response for H124 (R128: +0.322, +0.095 to +0.548) is strongly directionally consistent but its lower bound is just below the +0.10 benchmark, so I keep H124 accepted as a discovery-supported MTAP-loss context association, not as an independently benchmarked central claim. For the due H148 interaction (TP53 loss USP7 high mutation burden), discovery R146 was positive but crossed the benchmark (+0.222, +0.079 to +0.365), while validation R153 was negative and entirely below the benchmark (-0.165, -0.415 to +0.084). Combined evidence does not support a clinically meaningful positive modification, so I reject and close H148. Negative findings remain clear: KRAS mutation is not meaningfully associated with KRAS, RIT1, EGFR, or STAT3 dependency; BRAF V600E is not meaningfully associated with BRAF dependency; EGFR amplification is not meaningfully associated with EGFR, KRAS, or TMED10 dependency; ERBB2 amplification is not meaningfully associated with ERBB2 dependency; MYC amplification is not meaningfully associated with KIF18A, POLR2A, RPL11, DHX9, TMED10, or USP7 dependency; TP53 loss is not associated with MDM2 dependency; ARID1A loss is not associated with SMARCA2 dependency; MTAP loss is not associated with USP7 or MDM2 dependency; BRCA2 loss is not associated with WRN, DHX9, or POLR2A dependency; and constructed research-marker main effects are largely null. These nulls are absence of benchmark-crossing evidence in this dataset, not proof of absence. Residual uncertainty is mainly context attenuation or interaction, not main-effect existence: PTEN/STAT3 is unresolved in KY-library context (H96/R93) and TP53-loss context (H102/R99), low-burden PTEN/STAT3 is unresolved (H141/R135), WRN/MSI ARID1A interaction is unresolved but small (H142/R136), and several USP7/TP53 interaction checks remain unresolved/deferred (H145/R139, H154/R152, H112/R109, H129/R126). The most informative next analysis is focused validation or refined estimation of the borderline PTEN/STAT3 attenuation contexts: KY-library H96 first, then TP53-loss with CDKN2A-wild-type refinement H102. These should be accepted only if they cross +0.10 in a direction consistent with stronger dependency; otherwise they should be closed as context noise. No further validation of the five central associations is needed.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 13 final synthesis update. Central accepted and independently validated within-dataset associations: MSI-high stronger WRN (H6/R52), SMARCA4 loss stronger SMARCA2 (H8/R13), KEAP1 loss weaker NFE2L2 (H20/R39), TP53 loss weaker USP7 (H15/R26), PTEN loss stronger STAT3 (H93/R90). Operational rule: signed +0.10 benchmark, valid Welch cells, no causal or external-generalization claims. H124 accepted as MTAP-loss context-supported PTEN/STAT3 association; validation R128 is positive but lower bound +0.095 is just below +0.10, so treat as discovery-supported context, not independently benchmarked central. H148 now rejected/closed: high mutation burden does not support positive TP53/USP7 effect modification; R146 crossed benchmark while R153 was negative and below benchmark. ARID1A-loss main contexts H136-H139 accepted as context-supported; their interactions or redundant symmetric claims are generally rejected or low-priority. Remaining unresolved but low priority: H96 KY PTEN/STAT3, H102 TP53-loss PTEN/STAT3, H141 low-burden PTEN/STAT3, H142 WRN/MSI ARID1A interaction, H145 USP7/TP53 ARID1A interaction, H154 USP7/TP53 Avana interaction, H112 USP7/TP53 KEAP1 interaction, H129 USP7/TP53 CDKN2A interaction. Registered two refinements for next possible analysis: PTEN/STAT3 in KY and matched RNA-DNA-CRISPR QC, parent H96; and PTEN/STAT3 in TP53 loss with CDKN2A wild-type, parent H102. If continuing, prioritize H96 validation or refined estimation before broad new exploration because it is the clearest possible attenuation of an accepted central association."
}

