  "narrative": "All newly delivered context-robustness and specificity tests have valid Welch cells and can be judged against the +0.10 signed lower-bound benchmark. The PIK3CA-pathway context checks are decisive: TP53-loss cells continue to show a clinically meaningful weaker-dependency shift for dependency_USP7 in both PIK3CA-wildtype (H187, signed lower bound +0.314) and PIK3CA-mutant cells (H188, signed lower bound +0.238). KEAP1-loss continues to show clinically meaningful weaker dependency for dependency_NFE2L2 in both PIK3CA strata (H189 lower +0.770; H190 lower +0.769), and SMARCA4-loss continues to show clinically meaningful stronger dependency for dependency_SMARCA2 in both strata (H191 lower +0.763; H192 lower +0.735). These results support persistence of the central associations across common co-occurring PI3K-pathway context in this dataset. They are not interaction tests, so they do not prove equivalence between strata or absence of causal modification; however, the estimates are far from the clinical threshold and are consistent with previously validated main effects, so multiplicity is less concerning here.\n\nThe replication-stress/MYC checks are more informative for scope. Direct MYC amplification versus dependency_WRN (H195) gives a tiny signed effect of +0.033, 95% signed interval +0.002 to +0.064. Although the signed direction is favorable to more negative WRN dependency, the interval lies below the +0.10 clinical benchmark, so the claim of a clinically meaningful MYC-WRN association is rejected. In contrast, MSI-high remains strongly associated with dependency_WRN among MYC-nonamplified cells (H196, lower +0.763), KEAP1-loss remains strongly associated with weaker dependency_NFE2L2 among MYC-amplified cells (H197, lower +0.729), and PTEN-loss remains associated with stronger dependency_STAT3 among MYC-amplified cells (H198, lower +0.174). Thus the WRN effect is highly specific to MSI-high status rather than a broad MYC/replication-stress effect, and the KEAP1/NFE2L2 and PTEN/STAT3 associations remain clinically benchmarked in a MYC-amplified context.\n\nThe specificity checks also reject competing broad associations. BRCA2 loss is not clinically meaningfully associated with dependency_WRN in MSI-high-negative cells (H29, signed estimate +0.001, upper +0.032), supporting the view that the WRN association in this dataset is centered on MSI-high status rather than BRCA2 loss confounding. MYC amplification is not clinically meaningfully associated with dependency_SMARCA2 among SMARCA4-wildtype cells (H167, signed estimate +0.012, upper +0.014), supporting specificity of the SMARCA2 association for SMARCA4-loss context. These nulls do not prove exact zero or absence in all datasets; they indicate that, in this dataset, clinically meaningful effects are excluded by the 95% intervals at the chosen benchmark.\n\nNo independent validation is requested. The newly accepted claims are far from the +0.10 decision boundary or are supported by the same very large central effects already validated; the rejected claims are already bounded below the clinical benchmark, and validation of peripheral null or subgroup estimates would not materially change the central conclusions. The evidence continues to support within-dataset descriptive associations, not causality or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 17 appraise complete. PIK3CA-stratified robustness: central associations are accepted in both PIK3CA-wildtype and mutant strata for TP53-loss/USP7, KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2, and SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2. Myc context: MYC-WRN is rejected as clinically meaningful despite a tiny direction-consistent effect; MSI-WRN persists outside MYC; KEAP1/NFE2L2 and PTEN/STAT3 persist inside MYC. Specificity nulls: BRCA2/WRN in MSI-high-negative cells and MYC/SMARCA2 in SMARCA4-wildtype cells are rejected as clinically meaningful. Active central conclusions remain the five within-dataset associations: MSI-high -> stronger dependency_WRN, SMARCA4 loss -> stronger dependency_SMARCA2, KEAP1 loss -> weaker dependency_NFE2L2, TP53 loss -> weaker dependency_USP7, PTEN loss -> stronger dependency_STAT3. No causal or external-generalizability claim. Validation budget intentionally not used: new accepted effects are decisive and new rejects are already bounded below +0.10."
