  "narrative": "All 12 newly delivered discovery results are valid Welch comparisons and are judged against the pre-specified operational clinical benchmark: a signed 95% lower bound above +0.10 supports a clinically meaningful association or interaction in the registered direction, an interval whose upper bound is below +0.10 supports rejection, and an interval crossing +0.10 remains unresolved. H201 is accepted: TP53 loss gives a large weaker-dependency shift for dependency_USP7 in KEAP1-loss, non-PTEN-loss, non-SMARCA4-loss, non-MSI-high cells, signed estimate +0.466 with lower bound +0.280, well above threshold. H204 is accepted: PTEN loss gives a clinically meaningful stronger-dependency shift for dependency_STAT3 in clean TP53-wildtype, non-KEAP1-loss, non-SMARCA4-loss, non-MSI-high cells, lower bound +0.218. H205 is accepted: PTEN loss remains clinically meaningful among SMARCA4-loss cells, lower bound +0.118, supporting persistence of the PTEN-loss/STAT3 association in another co-mutation context. H207 is accepted: KEAP1 loss continues to give a very large weaker-dependency shift for dependency_NFE2L2 in MSI-high cells, lower bound +0.703. H208 is accepted: SMARCA4 loss continues to give a very large stronger-dependency shift for dependency_SMARCA2 in MYC-amplified cells, lower bound +0.759. These acceptances are far from the decision boundary except H205, and they reinforce central conclusions rather than create new peripheral claims. H202 is rejected: the PTEN-loss x TP53-loss interaction on dependency_STAT3 has a negative signed estimate in the registered direction and an upper bound of only +0.055, so a clinically meaningful favorable interaction is excluded, though this is a within-dataset effect-modification test and not a causal statement. H210 is rejected: KEAP1 loss is not clinically meaningfully associated with dependency_WRN, upper bound +0.037, which supports WRN specificity for MSI-high status. H199, H200, H206, and H209 are unresolved: their intervals cross zero and/or the +0.10 benchmark. H199 and H200 suggest that KEAP1-loss modification or independent association with dependency_USP7 in TP53-loss contexts is small and uncertain. H206 suggests TP53 loss may weaken dependency_USP7 in MSI-high cells, point estimate +0.310, but the 95% interval lower bound is -0.029 and the exposed cell is small, so this is not support for a clinically meaningful effect. H209 similarly suggests a possible small positive KEAP1-loss effect on dependency_USP7 among TP53-loss cells, lower bound -0.041, but this remains unresolved. I request independent validation for H203 because it tests the central PTEN-loss/STAT3 association in a stricter TP53-loss, non-KEAP1-loss, non-SMARCA4-loss, non-MSI-high context; its point estimate +0.186 is clinically suggestive but lower bound +0.038 is below the benchmark. This is the most useful validation target among the new results because a clean positive result would strengthen the central PTEN/STAT3 conclusion after controlling for other dominant co-mutational contexts, while failure would leave that stricter context unresolved without undermining the already accepted central association.",
